A signal lantern class chains its constructors as shown. What prints?
class Lantern { int glow; Lantern() { this(5); } Lantern(int g) { glow = g * 2; } }
Lantern l = new Lantern(); System.out.print(l.glow);

A mooring buoy class offers two ways to build as shown. What prints?
class Buoy { int depth = 3; Buoy() { depth = depth + 4; } Buoy(int d) { depth = d - 1; } }
Buoy b = new Buoy(9); System.out.print(b.depth);

A grain mill prices its work with a helper as shown. What prints?
class Mill { int grind(int grain) { return grain * 3; } void run() { System.out.print(grind(4) + 1); } }
new Mill().run();

A marching band turns up one drum through a helper as shown. What prints?
class Drum { int beats = 2; }
class Band { static void louder(Drum d) { d.beats = d.beats + 5; } public static void main(String[] args) { Drum d = new Drum(); louder(d); System.out.print(d.beats); } }

A weather mast reads through a guarded call as shown. What prints?
class Sensor { int read() throws java.io.IOException { throw new java.io.IOException(); } }
Sensor s = new Sensor(); try { s.read(); System.out.print(1); } catch (java.io.IOException e) { System.out.print(2); }

An orchard crate class chains its builders as shown. What value prints? Respond with the integer only.
class Crate { int apples; Crate() { this(4); } Crate(int a) { apples = a + 6; } }
Crate c = new Crate(); System.out.print(c.apples);

A weaving loom prices each run as shown. What value does the print show? Respond with the integer only.
class Loom { int weave(int threads) { return threads * 2 + 3; } }
System.out.print(new Loom().weave(6));

A coastal beacon chains three constructors as shown. What prints?
class Beacon { int range; Beacon() { this(3, 4); } Beacon(int a) { this(a, a + 1); } Beacon(int a, int b) { range = a * 10 + b; } }
System.out.print(new Beacon().range);

A parade cart is lent to a helper that swaps in a fresh cart as shown. What prints?
class Cart { int wheels = 4; }
static void swap(Cart c) { c = new Cart(); c.wheels = 8; }
Cart mine = new Cart(); swap(mine); System.out.print(mine.wheels);

A print press totals pages with a loop as shown. What prints?
class Press { int stamp(int pages) { int total = 0; for (int i = 1; i <= pages; i++) { total = total + i; } return total; } }
System.out.print(new Press().stamp(4));

A water tank is built empty and then topped up as shown. What prints?
class Tank { int liters; Tank() { liters = 5; } Tank(int l) { liters = l; } void add(int x) { liters = liters + x; } }
Tank t = new Tank(); t.add(9); System.out.print(t.liters);

A gauge builder expects 7 but the dial shows 0 as shown. Which repair works?
class Meter { int units; Meter(int units) { units = units; } }
Meter m = new Meter(7); System.out.print(m.units);

Two satchels share one canvas through assignment, then one tightens the other as shown. What value prints? Respond with the integer only.
class Satchel { int straps; Satchel() { this(2); } Satchel(int s) { straps = s * 3 + 1; } void tighten(Satchel other) { other.straps = other.straps - 2; } }
Satchel a = new Satchel(); Satchel b = a; b.tighten(a); System.out.print(a.straps);
